+	// sound on the same entity and channel starts, so a scene's overlapping lines on the player cut each
+	// other off. each delayed voice sound of the player gets a channel of its own; its stop and change
+	// messages follow it there. hl2dm-sp patches its x64 engine instead where it can; this tree's x86
+	// engine keeps the workaround
